  </div>
</div>

<!-- Critical Insight -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="insight-box">
    <h4>The Core Pricing Problem</h4>
    <p><strong>47.6% of all orders are ≤ ₹100</strong>, but they contribute only <strong>20% of revenue</strong>. Meanwhile, orders ≥ ₹300 are just 10.4% of orders but drive <strong>31.7% of revenue</strong>. The median order (₹110) is significantly lower than the average (₹151), meaning a long tail of small orders is pulling the center down. Your highest-volume item — Desi Indori Poha at ₹50 — sells ~2,245 units (the #1 item by a wide margin) but is priced below the threshold where it meaningfully contributes to margin. A ₹10 increase here alone would add ~₹22K over the period, or ~₹115/day.</p>
  </div>
</div>

